A widespread agricultural practice is an unexpected CO2 sink

‘Liming’ to reduce soil acidity has long been considered a carbon dioxide source, but in North America’s largest river basin, it has resulted in net capture of atmospheric carbon.






                    By

G. Philip Robertson ORCID: http://orcid.org/0000-0001-9771-98950 & 




                Stephen K. Hamilton ORCID: http://orcid.org/0000-0002-4702-90171

